DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvmm__ppaaggee__ggrraabb() function returns the page at _p_i_n_d_e_x from the given ob‐
     ject.  If the page exists and is busy, vvmm__ppaaggee__ggrraabb() will sleep while
     waiting for it.  If the page does not exist, it is allocated.  The func‐
     tion sleeps until the allocation request can be satisfied.

     The function requires the _o_b_j_e_c_t to be locked on entry, and returns with
     the object locked.  If the vvmm__ppaaggee__ggrraabb() function sleeps for any reason,
     the object lock is temporary dropped.

     The vvmm__ppaaggee__ggrraabb() supports all of the flags supported by
     vm_page_alloc(9).  In addition, vvmm__ppaaggee__ggrraabb() supports the following
     flags:

     VM_ALLOC_IGN_SBUSY  When waiting for the busy state of the existing page
                         to drain, only test for exclusive busy; ignore the
                         shared busy counter.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The vvmm__ppaaggee__ggrraabb() always returns the page.

